<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran signals satisfaction, skepticism after US midterm vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acf2be4288e34c6daed4513df1604169c5d33ce554783e3899963340e684e9ee</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149--f14e22022dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the Iranian regime says the US midterms will not change Washington's policy toward Tehran, some officials and commentators see the resounding Democratic victory as blowback against the Iran war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Trump's midterm elections loss mean for strained US-India ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13aaf55797ec72c1e56bbb94eb79e21a9452a69dc618fb3a998668d9f784f750</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777--7836c1679b1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's electoral setback might give New Delhi and Washington space to reset relations, but there is no guarantee that the US will actually change its approach to India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea tells EU to 'mind its own business' on human rights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1c63765b4d9732fbafc2e9b31199ce72af370a7131105097846e2241b7fd3cd</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-tells-eu-to-mind-its-own-business-on-human-rights/a-79862196--b096a2c3122f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-tells-eu-to-mind-its-own-business-on-human-rights/a-79862196?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's UN mission has lashed out at the European Union over a draft UN resolution. Pyongyang has said the West does not have a monopoly on human rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02cc59e70ebebd98bbea286f5220e6bfcd25278e40bf5bf3d48cc22e763eda</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: ​​Several feared trapped as building collapses in Old Delhi's Chawri Bazar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd824c70487c418ddf42a940bf79e4a9f6f34a2e9459116864bb3ca8efabe1b1</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-_several-feared-trapped-as-building-collapses-in-old-delhi-s-chawri-bazar/live-79860330--a1bf871f58da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-​​several-feared-trapped-as-building-collapses-in-old-delhi-s-chawri-bazar/live-79860330?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue operations are ongoing as a building collapsed in Chawri Bazaar. Meanwhile, "Ramayana," starring Ranbir Kapoor and Sai Pallavi, has hit theaters. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong sentenced to 10 more years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba57642ab22220dd338f0b1e023313afc176d265472916671a1d92dbf6f46d96</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-more-years/a-79859898--15d97090ad43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-more-years/a-79859898?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Wong, once a teen activist and one of the faces of the "Umbrella Movement," is spending years of his adult life in prison.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Swift space telescope plunges back to Earth in fiery demise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27a507487255eb502da9ef8185b4e9aaef0911cb172e5f341317d791f92a43f6</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T04:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-swift-space-telescope-plunges-back-to-earth-in-fiery-demise/a-79859805--86b86ba56b3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-swift-space-telescope-plunges-back-to-earth-in-fiery-demise/a-79859805?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">NASA's Swift orbital observatory fell back to Earth after running its mission for more than two decades. A rescue attempt to raise its sinking orbit had earlier failed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia deploys troops to Jakarta after wiretapping allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ede1faee7c5621110996e601dbd91931c5f3ae180d286060f8d01167429df915</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779--6f55d522a605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indonesian troops are being stationed in Jakarta amid wiretapping allegations implicating the president's chief of staff. Suspects are being accused of illegally tapping the president's phones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China and India achieved diplomatic thaw. Now the border is flaring up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d82016875cb7ea5fba8f1a0a5d96ab8ff674d8b9fd5df1156da5f825c02cc9a9</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-and-india-achieved-diplomatic-thaw-now-the-border-is-flaring-up/a-79843273--6b47f2ce5be9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-and-india-achieved-diplomatic-thaw-now-the-border-is-flaring-up/a-79843273?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities have confirmed a new border "face-off" between Indian and Chinese troops in Arunachal Pradesh, raising questions about the still fragile thaw in relations between New Delhi and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>8 ways the US midterm election could affect Donald Trump's Iran policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32e88a8b9031df3fcd76a56a87501df645c286f38c6d0c75aa425b089fa4bb4</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816--8cf7f9243f7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the US midterms could open a window for diplomacy with Iran, they could also unleash a new military escalation. DW spoke with analysts to identify eight factors that could tip the balance toward war or peace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02c897b1188dc56aa7635610b875c9a6ec585de865ac3bece95dbfaf201a41db</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a3279be22e5c6655d8f26cb67f0f70830893102ef42aad04dae0645476771f4</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e62592511b46894eb26c331111da9f059d08e18d792f188df6932faa2edbf0f</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
